# Client Code Quality

## Stack — current idioms only

React 19 · TS (strict) · Next.js 16 App Router · Tailwind v4 · Zustand v5 · Zod 4.

- Conversation / UI session state → Zustand (selectors; no server secrets inside).
- Coach API turns → feature hook calling `features/coach/api`. Not `useState`+`useEffect`+fetch soup.
- Forms / payloads → Zod schemas as source of truth; prefer `z.infer`.
- `useEffect` only for external systems (DOM focus, scroll); always clean up.
- Function components + hooks only. No class components, deprecated APIs, or `any`.

## CSS homes

- App tokens / `@theme` / shared utilities → `app/globals.css`.
- Coach desk atmosphere / feature composites → colocated CSS next to the feature (e.g. `features/coach/components/*.css`) or `styles/`.
- Do not keep appending large feature blobs into `globals.css`.

## DRY — single source of truth

Search before you write. Reuse or extend. Never paste a second copy of a type, constant, or behavior.

## Quality bar

- **≤ 350 lines/file.** Over → split.
- No `console.*`, commented-out code, dead code, or unused exports.
- A11y: semantic HTML, keyboard controls, `aria-label` on icon buttons, `aria-hidden` on decorative SVGs, visible focus, honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Path alias `@/` for cross-layer imports; relative only within a feature/folder.
- Naming: Components PascalCase; hooks `useX`; utils camelCase; scalars SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE; folders kebab-case.
- Before done: `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` must pass.

## Performance

- Subscribe to narrow Zustand slices.
- Keep message list simple until it grows long enough to virtualize.
